k Wilder to [[Sutos Island]] and took control of the Professor's castle as the new leader of the Organization. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}","text":"The Huntik team went to the Professor's castle in response to an invitation from the Professor, though they figured this invite to be a trap. Tricked by the Professor, Dante Vale parted with the Rings of the Legendary Titans Behemoth and Tao. [The Divine Comedy] Though confronted with Overlos, the Legendary Titan of Immortality, the Huntik Foundation defeated the Professor due to some quick thinking on the part of Lok Lambert and betrayal from Rassimov. [The Mission]\n\nAfter recruiting help from Grier, the Huntik team returned to the Professor's castle in order to recover Organization files about Rassimov. Unable to ally with the new head of the Organization, Wilder, Grier took Wilder to Sutos Island and took control of the Professor's castle as the new leader of the Organization. [An Ally from the Organization]"},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nCastle courtyard.jpg|Concept Art of the castle courtyard\nS1E10 Professors Castle.jpg|The Professor's castle\nS1E26_Professors_castle_2.jpg|The castle at night\nS1E26_Professors_castle.jpg|The castle with the lit window of the Professor's study\nS1E26_Professor_castle_Prague.jpg|The castle during the invocation of [[Overlos]]\nS1E26 Araknos Tao Behemoth ritual.jpg|The Professor's Invocation chamber\nS2E46 team Grier castle gate.png|Entrance\nS2E46 castle courtyard team.png|Castle courtyard\nS1E26 Zhalia King Basilisk Undergolem.jpg\nS1E25 Rassimov Dante Thornment Caliban.jpg\nS1E25 Dante Thornment.jpg\nS2E46 Professor's castle map.png|[[Teknonomicon]] display\n</gallery>\n[[Category:Locations]]\n[[Category:Prague, Czech Republic]]\n[[Category:Organization bases]]","text":"Castle courtyard.jpg|Concept Art of the castle courtyard\nS1E10 Professors Castle.jpg|The Professor's castle\nS1E26_Professors_castle_2.jpg|The castle at night\nS1E26_Professors_castle.jpg|The castle with the lit window of the Professor's study\nS1E26_Professor_castle_Prague.jpg|The castle during the invocation of Overlos\nS1E26 Araknos Tao Behemoth ritual.jpg|The Professor's Invocation chamber\nS2E46 team Grier castle gate.png|Entrance\nS2E46 castle courtyard team.png|Castle courtyard\nS1E26 Zhalia King Basilisk Undergolem.jpg\nS1E25 Rassimov Dante Thornment Caliban.jpg\nS1E25 Dante Thornment.jpg\nS2E46 Professor's castle map.png|Teknonomicon display"}],"full_text":"The Professor's castle is the castle where the Professor used to live. In addition to Organization Central, the Professor's castle was, and remained, one of the main bases of the Organization.\n== History ==\nThe Huntik team went to the Professor's castle in response to an invitation from the Professor, though they figured this invite to be a trap. Tricked by the Professor, Dante Vale parted with the Rings of the Legendary Titans Behemoth and Tao. [The Divine Comedy] Though confronted with Overlos, the Legendary Titan of Immortality, the Huntik Foundation defeated the Professor due to some quick thinking on the part of Lok Lambert and betrayal from Rassimov. [The Mission]\n\nAfter recruiting help from Grier, the Huntik team returned to the Professor's castle in order to recover Organization files about Rassimov. Unable to ally with the new head of the Organization, Wilder, Grier took Wilder to Sutos Island and took control of the Professor's castle as the new leader of the Organization. [An Ally from the Organization]\n\n== Gallery ==\n\nCastle courtyard.jpg|Concept Art of the castle courtyard\nS1E10 Professors Castle.jpg|The Professor's castle\nS1E26_Professors_castle_2.jpg|The castle at night\nS1E26_Professors_castle.jpg|The castle with the lit window of the Professor's study\nS1E26_Professor_castle_Prague.jpg|The castle during the invocation of Overlos\nS1E26 Araknos Tao Behemoth ritual.jpg|The Professor's Invocation chamber\nS2E46 team Grier castle gate.png|Entrance\nS2E46 castle courtyard team.png|Castle courtyard\nS1E26 Zhalia King Basilisk Undergolem.jpg\nS1E25 Rassimov Dante Thornment Caliban.jpg\nS1E25 Dante Thornment.jpg\nS2E46 Professor's castle map.png|Teknonomicon display","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox location\n| image       = S1E18 Professors Castle.jpg\n| type        = Castle\n| level       = 2\n| location    = [[Prague, Czech Republic]]\n| inhabitants = [[The Professor]] (formerly) <br> [[Rassimov]] (formerly) <br> [[Wilder]] (formerly) <br> [[Eathon the dog]] <br> [[Hoffman]] <br> [[Suits]]\n|first appearance = \"[[The Beautiful Trap]]\"\n}}'''The Professor's castle''' is the castle where [[the Professor]] used to live. In addition to [[Organization Central]], the Professor's castle was, and remained, one of the main bases of [[the Organization]].\n== History ==\nThe [[Huntik Foundation|Huntik]] team went to the Professor's castle in response to an invitation from the Professor, though they figured this invite to be a trap. Tricked by the Professor, [[Dante Vale]] parted with the [[Rings]] of the [[Legendary Titans]] [[Behemoth]] and [[Tao]]. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} Though confronted with [[Overlos]], the Legendary Titan of Immortality, the Huntik Foundation defeated the Professor due to some quick thinking on the part of [[Lok Lambert]] and betrayal from [[Rassimov]]. {{source|The Mission}}\n\nAfter recruiting help from [[Grier]], the Huntik team returned to the Professor's castle in order to recover Organization files about [[Rassimov]]. Unable to ally with the new head of the Organization, [[Wilder]], Grier took Wilder to [[Sutos Island]] and took control of the Professor's castle as the new leader of the Organization. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}\n\n== Gallery ==\n{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nCastle courtyard.jpg|Concept Art of the castle courtyard\nS1E10 Professors Castle.jpg|The Professor's castle\nS1E26_Professors_castle_2.jpg|The castle at night\nS1E26_Professors_castle.jpg|The castle with the lit window of the Professor's study\nS1E26_Professor_castle_Prague.jpg|The castle during the invocation of [[Overlos]]\nS1E26 Araknos Tao Behemoth ritual.jpg|The Professor's Invocation chamber\nS2E46 team Grier castle gate.png|Entrance\nS2E46 castle courtyard team.png|Castle courtyard\nS1E26 Zhalia King Basilisk Undergolem.jpg\nS1E25 Rassimov Dante Thornment Caliban.jpg\nS1E25 Dante Thornment.jpg\nS2E46 Professor's castle map.png|[[Teknonomicon]] display\n</gallery>\n[[Category:Locations]]\n[[Category:Prague, Czech Republic]]\n[[Category:Organization bases]]","categories":["Locations","Organization bases","Prague, Czech Republic"],"links":[{"target_title":"Prague, Czech Republic","label":"Prague, Czech Republic","target_id":"huntik:page:8072","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Prague%2C_Czech_Republic","status":"resolved","href":"#/categories?name=Prague%2C%20Czech%20Republic"},{"target_title":"The Professor","label":"The Professor","target_id":"huntik:page:2053","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Professor","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2053"},{"target_title":"Rassimov","label":"Rassimov","target_id":"huntik:page:2090","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Rassimov","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2090"},{"target_title":"Wilder","label":"Wilder","target_id":"huntik:page:4467","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Wilder","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4467"},{"target_title":"Eathon the dog","label":"Eathon the dog","target_id":"huntik:page:3517","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Eathon_the_dog","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3517"},{"target_title":"Hoffman","label":"Hoffman","target_id":"huntik:page:4577","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Hoffman","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4577"},{"target_title":"Suits","la